  "implementation_invariants": [
    "Both model outputs are parsed as one complete JSON document under document_parser; substring or regex JSON extraction is forbidden.",
    "Stage A output has exactly one top-level key: intents.",
    "Stage A decline is exactly {\"intents\":[]} and terminates Stage A processing.",
    "intended_hold_days is required and must be no greater than target_dte.",
    "side=debit permits only long call, long put, call debit spread, or put debit spread.",
    "side=credit permits only cash secured put and direction=bullish.",
    "call structures require direction=bullish; put debit structures require direction=bearish.",
    "The model never emits est_debit_usd, price, strike, expiry, con_id, width, or quantity in Stage A.",
    "Runtime assigns intent IDs by Stage A array order: intent_1 through intent_3.",
    "Runtime creates candidate_id as cand_ plus the full lowercase SHA-256 of canonical JSON containing contract_version, intent_id, underlying, side, direction, structure, expiry, and ordered leg economic identities {con_id, action, right, strike}.",
    "Every candidate_id within one Stage B input is distinct; duplicate candidate economic identities are rejected before Stage B.",
    "Stage B receives 3 to 5 candidates that all match its intent_id, underlying, side, direction, and structure.",
    "Every Stage B candidate passed fresh two-sided quote, structure, DTE, liquidity, affordability, and live-cap checks before model exposure.",
    "liquidity_status=pass means every leg has positive bid_per_share and ask_per_share, combo bid and ask are positive, and bid_ask_spread_pct is within the configured entry spread limit; bid_ask_spread_pct is the v2 declared liquidity metric.",
    "For debit candidates, dte is at least intended_hold_days times the conviction multiplier: 8 for conviction 1 through 6, 6 for 7, 5 for 8, and 4 for 9 through 10. Four times intended hold is the absolute debit floor.",
    "For cash-secured-put candidates, dte is within the configured 3 through 45 day credit window and no shorter than intended_hold_days.",
    "A debit candidate has one_contract_credit_usd=null. A cash-secured-put candidate has width_usd=null, exactly one sell put leg, and non-null one_contract_credit_usd.",
    "A long call has exactly one buy call leg; a long put has exactly one buy put leg; a debit spread has ordered buy then sell legs of the structure's right and a non-null positive width_usd.",
    "For every debit candidate, one_contract_cost_usd equals combo_ask_per_share times 100 and one_contract_max_loss_usd equals one_contract_cost_usd.",
    "For a debit spread, 0 < combo_ask_per_share <= width_usd and one_contract_max_loss_usd equals one_contract_cost_usd.",
    "For a cash secured put, one_contract_cost_usd equals strike times 100 and one_contract_max_loss_usd equals one_contract_cost_usd minus one_contract_credit_usd.",
    "Stage B selection is valid only when candidate_id exactly matches one supplied candidate; runtime binds the selected ordered con_ids and may never silently substitute a different contract on refresh.",
    "Stage B decline is exactly {\"decline\":true}, contains no rationale field, and terminates processing for that intent.",
    "Runtime computes quantity and quoted totals after Stage B, then requotes the exact selected con_ids and revalidates candidate identity, two-sided executable price, width, account state, and caps before approval and again before submission. If the selected candidate fails, runtime declines rather than reselecting silently.",
    "If fewer than 3 candidates survive prefiltering, runtime does not call Stage B and declines that intent.",
    "Continuous, daily-slate, and add-name paths use this same contract, units, candidate builder, and revalidation ownership."
  ],
